= Online platform — Technical =

Platform architectures commonly combine identity, storage, ranking, APIs, policy enforcement, analytics, and interaction surfaces. Technical affordances and governance rules jointly shape which interactions are possible, visible, amplified, restricted, or monetized.

== Modeling / implementation cautions ==
* online platform ≠ Internet
* platform ≠ protocol
* platform rules ≠ technical protocol rules

== References ==
* Tarleton Gillespie, ''Custodians of the Internet'' (2018), platform governance and moderation.
* José van Dijck, Thomas Poell, and Martijn de Waal, ''The Platform Society'' (2018).
* OECD digital-platform literature, for platform-mediated interactions and ecosystems.
